parameter set deepseek-v4-pro, reviewed 2026-10-08
  DeepSeek V4 Pro (deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro) from its published configuration: 61 layers: 30 Compressed Sparse Attention layers (compression ratio 4, lightning indexer top-k 1,024) and 31 Heavily Compressed Attention layers (ratio 128, dense over the compressed entries), each with a 128-token sliding branch; 128 query heads over one shared 512-wide key-value vector, stored in FP8 with BF16 rotary dimensions (448 + 64 x 2 = 576 bytes per entry); FP4 indexer, 64 heads x 128. The multi-token prediction layer and hyper-connections are not counted.
  a_p, uJ per pair    0.0471 / 0.0471 / 0.09892 / 0.1507 / 0.1507  D
  a_d, uJ per pair    0.1037 / 0.1037 / 0.1747 / 0.2744 / 0.2744  D
  b_in, J per token   0.1573 / 0.1573 / 0.2086 / 0.3208 / 0.3208  D
  b_out, J per token  0.2567 / 0.2567 / 0.3377 / 0.5194 / 0.5194  D
  c0, mJ per token    0.000446 / 0.000446 / 0.0008919 / 0.001338 / 0.001338  D
  idle                1 / 1 / 1.12 / 1.35 / 1.9  D

parameter set deepseek-v4.1-flash, reviewed 2026-10-08
  DeepSeek V4.1 Flash (deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash) from its published configuration: 40 layers: layers 0 and 1 sliding only (window 128); 18 encoder layers with compression ratio 2 and 20 decoder layers uncompressed, all with top-k 512 and the 128-token sliding branch; 64 query heads over one shared 512-wide key-value vector; global KV cache 890 bytes per token over the model, FP4 with E4M3 scales (taken as 890 / 38 = 23.4 bytes per entry per layer); indexer 32 heads x 128 at FP4 in the 8 index-source layers. Not modelled: the Reuse and Reindex modes, the encoder-decoder prefill shortcut and Engram memory, which overstates prefill attention.
  a_p, uJ per pair    0.006656 / 0.006656 / 0.01398 / 0.0213 / 0.0213  D
  a_d, uJ per pair    0.0624 / 0.0624 / 0.0936 / 0.1498 / 0.1498  D
